// Varmak Workshop backend — Phase 0A schema, corrected in Phase 0A-R1.
// Implements the approved Backend Architecture Contract (Decisions 1-9).
// Schema only: no seed data, no business logic. See backend/README.md.
//
// Conventions applied throughout, per the contract's Database Rules:
// - Every model has a database-native UUID primary key (gen_random_uuid(), Postgres 13+ built-in),
//   without exception. Prior to Phase 0A-R1, InventoryItem and BarcodeLink used their human-readable
//   business key (`code`, `barcode`) as the primary key itself — corrected: both now have a real
//   `id` UUID primary key, with `code`/`barcode` demoted to a separate unique business-key column,
//   and every relationship that referenced them now uses a real UUID foreign key
//   (`inventoryItemId`), never the business code.
// - Every human-readable business identifier — "no" fields, and business keys like
//   InventoryItem.code, BarcodeLink.barcode, Equipment.equipmentId, Offcut.code — is a separate,
//   uniquely-indexed column, never the primary key and never used as a relationship target.
// - timestamptz for events/instants; plain `Date` (@db.Date) for calendar dates.
// - Decimal (never Float) for money, quantities, rates and measured values.
// - Currency is stored explicitly beside every monetary field.
// - No polymorphic entityType/entityId soft links, with one explicitly-justified exception:
//   AuditLog.entityType is a label used only for filtering/display, never a join or an
//   authorization decision — see the comment on AuditLog below. SafetyEvent's prior use of the
//   same pattern was removed in Phase 0A-R1 in favor of explicit typed foreign keys (see the
//   comment on SafetyEvent below) — SafetyEvent has none of this exception left.
// - onDelete: Restrict on every relation in this schema — nothing cascades. This is a deliberate,
//   conservative default consistent with the app's "archive, never hard-delete" convention; it can
//   be relaxed later, per relation, with explicit review once real deletion workflows exist.
// - createdAt/updatedAt on every mutable model. `version` (optimistic concurrency) on entities with
//   meaningful concurrent-edit risk, matching the stale-index race class documented in the
//   frontend audit (Pass 3.27). Immutable/append-only models (SafetyEvent, QualityRelease) omit
//   `updatedAt` entirely and are enforced insert-only at the database level — see their comments.
// - Actor references (who performed an action) are real, named, indexed foreign keys to User —
//   e.g. PurchaseRequisition.requestedById/approvedById, QualityHold.appliedById/releasedById,
//   EquipmentBreakdown.resolvedById, QualityRelease.releasedById,
//   MigrationReconciliationRecord.resolvedById — never a bare, unrelated UUID column.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../src/generated/prisma"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

